{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c959","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3be-22c5-72c2-9a68-fcdf0b06f553"},"sequence":775,"recorded_at":1780531400001545,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4c090c0f-8ac7-469e-b4bd-d568cdc91e07","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4c090c0f-8ac7-469e-b4bd-d568cdc91e07","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4c090c0f-8ac7-469e-b4bd-d568cdc91e07"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3c1-62be-74f3-b4d8-c5655ed6405c"},"task_id":"01a0b3c1-62be-74f3-b4d8-c5655ed6405c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3c1-62be-74f3-b4d8-c5655ed6405c","chunk":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-18\n7|\n8|### TASK-260830-2056mm — Terminal binding events and recovery (story-final leaf)\n9|- DELIVERED: `internal/termbind` — the §4.1/4.B-4.D/5.2-Terminal-Events/7.A final leaf over the landed owners and the story's own `axpane`/`terminstance`: `ParseTerminalBinding` owns the Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed object no parser existed for (ID recomputed before use, construction byte-agreed with the landed manifest admission); `CheckInstanceIdentity` + the operation-body pre-scans refuse the eight forbidden identity forms with the pinned protocol class on the Binding, descriptor (adopted landed entry), operation bodies, bootstrap binding, and attach receipts, with the CLI Result 4 surface a tripwire-pinned bound; `ResolveEvidence` resolves each v4 event's evidence IDs to exactly one Manifest, one Probe, and the Capability Evidence objects bound to the event tuple through the landed `Registry.AdmitProbe` (eleven foreign resolution targets refuse, substitution fails closed); `EmitTerminalCreated`/`EmitResumed` author the v4 payloads under a locally held lease with the digest as the opaque reference; `RecoverCreate` is read-only (absence / ONE child / unavailable+status_first, window from the fold newest); the attach receipt store records one durable receipt per client pair and emits neither event. Takeover selects an admitted backend with a new digest and event, append-only, never a fork; v1 readers stay inert.\n10|- F1: the producer's \"§13.1\" recovery rule lives at §4.1 lines 1395/1399 in the pinned v0.7.0 document (\"status plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one child\") — §13.1's eight measured clauses are launch-plan/boot-direct/argv rules owned by another story, so the registry binds `section:4.1` (new, sliver 1/5) and leaves `section:13.1` untouched, with the mapping stated in the results.\n11|- F2: a pre-scan gate is masked wherever the landed parser refuses with the identical code — the descriptor surface needed no wrapper (landed `AdmitProviderDescriptor` already pins `terminal_backend_protocol_error`), while the mutation-context/status/bootstrap surfaces needed one (landed plain refusals), and same-code reroutes (transport enum, evidence protocol arm, foreign-kind classification) need detail assertions or the mutant survives behind the landed twin.\n12|- F3: the registry needed a reviewed-new-bindings extension — `assertNewBindingsAreReviewed` admitted only unevidenced stubs for sections the trunk baseline never bound, so `section:4.1` carries proof through a new `storyNewV070Bindings` list with literal matching plus clause remeasurement, mirroring the existing upgrade lists; seven new acceptance cases, four upgraded bindings (4.B/4.D/5.2 slivers, 7.A partial), digest re-pinned, tracecheck `63/574`.\n13|- CLOSED the inherited residuals: axpane P3-1/P3-4/P3-5 (journal-only restore closure witness, the `EmitParked` winning-lease production binding with the mandated fix, corrupt-blob witness; the losing-lease test keeps its assertions with consistent-winner fixtures) and terminstance P3-1..P3-4 (five reviewer witnesses verbatim, three enum corpora extended, six mirrored rows); P3-2/P3-3 stated as owner bounds (pure-`Decide` unreachable shape; remote-owner closure-first failure, fail-closed).\n14|- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 28 narrowing mutants plus one supplementary arm-delete row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 30/30 with the harmless SURVIVED control), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits, production blobs byte-identical. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text. Extended batteries green: axpane 56/56 twice, terminstance 122/122.\n15|- AC: 60 of 60 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via real SIGKILL on the attach and lost-create seams plus append-hook abort/replay. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n16|\n17|### TASK-260830-kkh1an rev4 — Terminal Instance rework: grant-less fencing verdict, expiry recheck, P3 arms\n18|- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev3 (no P1; P2 F3 production, P2 E3 evidence, 5 P3; the reviewer confirmed F1/F2/E1/E2 closed, the harness 100/100 twice, the 84/84 ratio, and a green suite — all kept untouched): F3 lands the exported `fencing.StaleRelativeToWinner` verdict (direction/tuple arms over a verified well-formed winner, no grant precondition — a grant authorizes, it never decides staleness) and composes it in `ObserveFencing` for grant-gated refusals, so the no-grant, lapsed-grant, no-clock and unusable-policy members fence from active/parked/quiescing under local and remote winners while unverified/ambiguous/winnerless/malformed/handoff-failed stay no-transition with the gate's own refusal or park; E3 commits the auth-expiry recheck witness (mid-operation expiry caught after one committed effect) plus a harness row that keeps the tuple recheck and drops the expiry recheck, and re-keys both E1 expired members onto the late-deadline instant so they kill on the receipt; P3-1..P3-4 commit the four reviewer witnesses with mirror rows, and P3-5 states the interim-proven create member with its `unavailable → terminate-stale` exit route.\n19|- F1: the grant-precondition class is exactly four members (no grant, no clock reading, lapsed grant, unusable policy) because those are all four refusals `Authorize` can surface after the ownership arms pass — the verdict decides the tuple fact for all four uniformly by never consulting grant/clock/policy, so completeness is structural, not enumerated, and the relative question needs no fallback (same grant facts, and the grant arms do not read `LocalHostID`).\n20|- F2: a narrowing row that spans a definition and its use is one plant, not two — the E3 row captures the entry instant and passes it to the in-loop authorization check, and either half alone breaks the build, so the kill measures the pair (same precedent as the rev3 resumption row spanning two adjacent checks).\n21|- F3: a grammar arm masked by a downstream arm is unmeasurable alone — the verdict's presented-session grammar arm needed the agreed-malformed member (both sides naming one malformed session, so only the grammar arm undecides it) because any other malformed session mismatches first.\n22|- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 114 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 116/116 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after/across. The eleven verdict rows mutate the landed package and are killed through `ObserveFencing`, so the composition — not the helper — is measured. The five surviving rev3 reviewer narrowings (RV3-M1/M2/M3/M4/M8) are mirrored as committed rows with committed killers; RV3-M6/M7 were already killed by the committed suite. Retired `N-fencing-epoch-only` (provably equivalent post-fix: a stale park implies a decided-stale verdict and both arms call `fenceLive` with the same refusal) and re-keyed `N-fencing-operation` to the non-live killer (launch-class now shows on the surfaced park vocabulary). No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\n23|- AC: 93 of 93 rows driven through production entries by named tests (rows 1–84 keep rev3 numbers; rows 85–93 are the rework rows; matrix in `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence carried from rev3 (no new durable write — the verdict and the recheck are pure over their inputs). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n24|\n25|### TASK-260830-kkh1an rev3 — Terminal Instance rework: resumption, remote fencing, row gates\n26|- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev2 (no P1; P2 F1/F2 production, P2 E1/E2 evidence, 7 P3; the rest — harness 70/70, 72/72 ratio, real-kill seam, hygiene — reproduced by the reviewer): F1 makes the same-key retry after `status` executable — a bound key without its completion reconciles through the production status entry, resumes under the same receipt when status proves the source (quiesce, stop-not-closed, create-absent: one effect set, one completion, one receipt), and refuses uncertain on target/contradiction/unknown; F2 fences the stale incarnation under a remote winner by asking the landed gate from the winner's own host (no local tuple comparison), from active/parked/quiescing, keeping the winning token as no-transition; E1 pins the create row's entry auth/generation/headless gates (no receipt bound) plus the committed second-effect timeout; E2 rotates lease+generation before the third stop effect and drifts the reported session on both status paths plus all five other axes both ways; P3-1 restores the source on pre-link store failure (post-link/lookup failures fence uncertain); P3-2 bounds fencing sources to the live states; P3-3 pins the deadline instant on both entries; P3-4 adds attach/none to the kind negatives; P3-6 replaces the kind twin with a landed `TransitionAuthorization` accessor (registered in the backend's census/inventory/audit batteries); P3-7 and `holder_host_id`-unbound recorded as stated leaf contracts.\n27|- REVERSAL (F2 of the rev2 entry, stated explicitly): \"pending-without-done is the honest interrupted state and its retry refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable`\" is FALSE as of rev3 for the proven-source case — the retry now reconciles through status and resumes under the same receipt when status proves the source, refusing uncertain only while the observation is genuinely unknown (target/contradiction/read-failure). TRACEABILITY rows 70/71 reworded to the resumed behavior; the `StoreHooks` doc sentence now states reconcile-instead-of-replay.\n28|- F1: an uncertain retry must reconcile through the production status entry rather than accept a caller-supplied report — a cached proof would let a stale source authorize a re-issue, while the engine's own exact-instance read cannot go stale; the query binds all six identity axes so a lying backend cannot authorize a resumption, and re-issue under the same key relies on the backend's own key binding (§13.13 safe_retry: never a second key, never a second process).\n29|- F2: the landed gate's arm order (\"the operative fact beats the credential\") hides staleness under a remote winner behind `remote_owner`, so the projection must ask twice — once as the local host, once relative to the winner — and fence only when the relative verdict is stale; both questions stay inside `fencing.Authorize`, which is composition, not a second model.\n30|- F3: the resumption's `err != nil` and `report.State != source` checks are one behavioral arm in two adjacent checks (status returns the empty report on every error path), so its narrowing row spans both and admits exactly the timeout-coded failed read; either half patched alone is masked by the other.\n31|- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 98 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 100/100 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after/across. The eleven rev2 reviewer narrowings are mirrored as committed rows with committed killers. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\n32|- AC: 84 of 84 rows driven through production entries by named tests (rows 1–72 keep rev2 numbers with 70/71 reworded; rows 73–84 are the rework rows; matrix in `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-SIGKILL pattern on both the quiesce and create seams, each extended through status-gated same-key resumption. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n33|\n34|### TASK-260830-kkh1an — Terminal Instance lifecycle execution engine (second leaf)\n35|- DELIVERED: `internal/terminstance` — the §4.C execution layer over the landed `terminalbackend` core: closed `AXAuthorization` (UUIDv4 lease, uint53 epoch bound, UUIDv7 holder, kind, timestamps, digest) through the `environ` closed-shape discipline, closed `RetryDisposition`/`ProviderProofKind` enums, the `MutationContext`/`MutationResult` identity contract with exact per-row idempotency material, and the `Engine` (durable receipt before first effect, per-effect auth+generation rechecks, source restore pre-commit, `unavailable`+`status_first` post-commit, deadline cancels waiting never committed effects). `stale_fenced` enters only through `fencing` park vocabulary; status is receipt/effect-free and unknown is never absent. Second leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\n36|- REFRESH: rev1 was constructed on `e6fe5c5` and its suite stopped at command 4/30 on the trunk resumesmoke time bomb (fixed as `a12d1bd`); this run refreshed the candidate onto `c3aae73` (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay, 29 stale trunk-changed paths restored to the new HEAD, LOGBOOK/README/decide.go rebased purely additive, `task-board.config.json` byte-identical), inherited the rev1 worktree delta verbatim, and re-verified it against SPEC.v0.7.0 plus the landed owners instead of redoing it.\n37|- F1: quiesce-input and request-stop carry no conditional beyond conferral — their spec capabilities are their sole conferring registry rows — so the landed `CheckOperation` decides those rows alone and a second arm restating it would be dead code; the engine's conditional covers only create-headless, wait-safe-plus-provider-iff, and status-provider, where the spec demands more than conferral.\n38|- F2: the receipt's no-replace commit needs a separate completion file, because the result is unknown at bind time and updating the receipt in place would break no-replace; pending-without-done is therefore the honest interrupted state and its retry refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable` with `status_first` instead of replaying or inventing absence.\n39|- F3: the epoch high edge cannot be weakened past `environ`'s own uint53 ceiling (same value, equivalent mutant), so that harness row tightens instead and proves the edge is exactly 9007199254740991 by refusing it; the min edge, the delegate's ceiling, and the tightening row triangulate the bound.\n40|- F4: closed P3-6 from the predecessor review (the `Decision.Descriptor` doc now states the recorded Binding instance is authoritative on reattach); P3-2/P3-3 stated as unreachable-shape bounds (no `Decide` caller, no checkpoint loader in this package); P3-1/P3-4/P3-5 left to the final leaf with the recovery/events reasons.\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
