{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd55","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3be-22c5-72c2-9a68-fcdf0b06f553"},"sequence":1285,"recorded_at":1780531400002565,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4c090c0f-8ac7-469e-b4bd-d568cdc91e07","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4c090c0f-8ac7-469e-b4bd-d568cdc91e07","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4c090c0f-8ac7-469e-b4bd-d568cdc91e07"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3c5216670c2971649de8eedf60a","text":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-18\n-\n-### TASK-260830-2056mm — Terminal binding events and recovery (story-final leaf)\n+## 2026-09-18\n+\n+### TASK-260830-2056mm rev2 — Race-gate rework: per-subtest evidence universes\n+- REWORKED after the rev1 CR validation stopped at command 5/30 (`go test ./... -race`): one DATA RACE in `TestResolveEvidenceRequiresManifestAndProbe` — four parallel subtests shared a single `mapUniverse` while the two \"second\" cases extended it, racing the sibling `Lookup` reads (`resolve_test.go:172/181` vs `fixtures_test.go:490`). The race detector then failed the whole `termbind` package; every other package was green. Fix is test-only: each subtest builds its own `universeMap(t, world)` copy (rev2 delta vs the rev1 candidate is exactly this hunk, proven by whole-tree diff of the reconstructed rev1 tree). No production byte changed; the `N-resolve-manifest-count` killer still kills its narrowing mutant.\n+- VERIFIED: `go test ./internal/termbind/ -race -count=10` green (plus two more `-count=3` passes), siblings `axpane`/`terminstance` `-race` green, `mutant_harness.py` 30/30 on two identical passes, gofmt/vet/build clean, `task-board.config.json` byte-identical, trunk still `c3aae73` (no refresh). Full 30-command suite reruns automatically at handoff.\n+- F1: a shared mutable map across `t.Parallel()` subtests fails the entire package under `-race`, not just the racing test — every concurrently running test reports \"race detected during execution of test\", so one fixture race reads as fifteen failures. Fixture isolation per subtest is the fix; read-only sharing (as in `TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds`) stays safe.\n+\n+### TASK-260830-2056mm — Terminal binding events and recovery (story-final leaf)\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"LOGBOOK.md","added":8,"removed":3},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
