{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cf8f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3be-22c5-72c2-9a68-fcdf0b06f553"},"sequence":1570,"recorded_at":1780531400003135,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4c090c0f-8ac7-469e-b4bd-d568cdc91e07","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"4c090c0f-8ac7-469e-b4bd-d568cdc91e07","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4c090c0f-8ac7-469e-b4bd-d568cdc91e07"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\n## What this run was\n\nThis was an autonomous-recovery rework run, not a fresh implementation. Rev1's CR validation stopped at command 5/30 (the `-race` gate) with a `DATA RACE` in `internal/termbind`, failing the whole package. The rev1 deliverable itself was intact.\n\n## Root cause and fix\n\n`TestResolveEvidenceRequiresManifestAndProbe` shared one `mapUniverse` across four `t.Parallel()` subtests while two of them extended it — concurrent map read/write (`resolve_test.go:172/181` vs `fixtures_test.go:490`), which failed all 15 concurrently-running termbind tests. Fix (test-only): each subtest builds its own `universeMap(t, world)` copy in [resolve_test.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree/internal/termbind/resolve_test.go:151). Audited the rest of the package: all other parallel subtests already isolate fixtures, and `Registry.AdmitProbe` is mutex-guarded.\n\nWhole-tree proof: reconstructed the rev1 candidate and diffed recursively — exactly 2 files differ (the fix hunk + a LOGBOOK rev2 entry). Zero production bytes changed.\n\n## Verification (all exit 0, logs attached)\n\n- `go test ./internal/termbind/ -race -count=10` green, plus two `-count=3` passes\n- `axpane` + `terminstance` `-race` green\n- termbind mutant harness 30/30 on two byte-identical passes, including verbose re-kill of `N-resolve-manifest-count` whose killer is the edited test\n- gofmt/vet/build clean, `task-board.config.json` byte-identical, trunk still c3aae73 (no refresh needed), no `__pycache__`\n\nCoverage stays 60/60 — no test added, removed, or renamed, so the rev1 conformance matrix stands. Full 30-command suite reruns automatically with the rev2 CR.\n\nAttached: `TASK-260830-2056mm_results-rev2.md` and `TASK-260830-2056mm_producer-evidence-rev2.tar.gz` (verified gzip). Handoff result: `status:to-review checklist:14/14`.","reason":null}}
